{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:cb19f7146b803c04638692cf162135e3f4f805fa770926c156c6d227054a79cb","title":"What information must a candidate physical theory contain before observational evidence can discriminate it from alternatives? The framework requires a specified prior, a physical description of the data, and calculable observation likelihoods for each candidate.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0000"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cbd702f82371ad014cb7ec5c81f7898c4b3756d945b15b501352ba90056e1b6d","title":"How can topological strings with dual open descriptions receive nonperturbative completions, and how should the resulting contour-dependent blocks map to Liouville conformal blocks in the logarithmic-matrix-model realization of AGT?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0010"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb8d828a1208bc56dd18cb564739142668844dff064eb4d77faef326c7cd856b","title":"How can F-theory describe geometrically massive diagonal D7-brane U(1)s and their gauge fluxes, including Stückelberg gaugings, tadpoles and induced chirality?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0011"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb79c8d07351af76caad941f79bbf06c2cd967ac5af504fda806682d51cf7868","title":"Can angular motion of a wrapped D5-brane near the warped resolved-conifold tip realize Natural Inflation with a Planckian decay constant while retaining control over backreaction?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cbf855f1b6005dcad3a8634ba4e3ab53846a4fcc354c30594b3b3999f3d24ab1","title":"Do minimally coupled scalars and fermions preserve an attractive gravitational UV fixed point when Newton's coupling is extracted from dynamical correlation functions, and what matter-content conclusions survive regulator validity bounds?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0020"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cbfdc3259d2aee1eba2e45d93ff361a183036b55bb52c966698fc21a701c5ffd","title":"What is the leading exponential suppression of thermal Schwinger pair production at arbitrary charge coupling in weak external fields, and what inclusive fixed-energy rates follow?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0024"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb6ff177c43b070d1a28edfb7f82fdd35dd4ffe8b1f2dd859993a2e165ee4063","title":"What minimal five-dimensional supersymmetric dilaton-gravity theory reproduces the linear-dilaton toy model of the holographic dual of Little String Theory, and what supersymmetry and four-dimensional spectrum does its background preserve?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cba697f61769b347eec12dbfae95a18f946156cec919565df140dd0c792b80f8","title":"How do analyticity, causality, and spectral unitarity constrain higher-point derivative operators, and how are those constraints related to energy conditions and the Legendre transform?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cbf2f2790a4b2713b8221b6bbabb025eb967ff5b25b43c932b9be935a99fe6a6","title":"Can dissipation complement brane corrections or modified kinetic terms that already permit steeper potentials? The paper presents this as an additional route beyond its canonical quartic examples.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0033"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cbe12ad8d5a002faddef6015437f31d690f43bb02b5917c18424db605bb912a0","title":"Can a thermal effective theory describing oscillatory reheating satisfy the conjectured restrictions on scalar potentials and field excursions? The paper compares this issue with warm inflation, in which interactions generate radiation during the inflationary stage.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0038"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb1d99e74d4a717302689bfbde357d693a9e0fc55bb2a279db10efe183296d4c","title":"Can derivative interactions and non-minimal gravitational coupling permit a viable dark-energy history with an order-one potential slope? The paper addresses this in one selected Horndeski ansatz by comparing cosmological histories with reconstructed equation-of-state constraints.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0038"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb1fdf169d94d0179508f3e7a1c385fa5c835d55e56a53a7ddc7286fbf82970a","title":"Can classical type II supergravity with Op/Dp sources support four-dimensional de Sitter spacetime? The paper fixes a commonly used smeared compactification ansatz to formulate existence, stability, and string-control questions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cbb701371bfff8799687b11c7e2ae173eb77790e8695364fc0d41555c86df4ac","title":"How can quantum gravity constrain an effective theory below its apparent cutoff? A Swampland scale indicates when modification becomes necessary for eventual completion, even when no immediate inconsistency occurs at that energy.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0040"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb1cde6a6587f290b1639decdb97c0cd316198529441e90091a91da6778f519f","title":"When do gravitational causality constraints on massive higher-spin particles apply to composites, and what bounds follow for confining large N gauge theories coupled to Einstein gravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cbf3938bc41c12f9de39ad4d0c7302e9957c3b9281f9cfa0935c44800cb99909","title":"Could hidden bound states in the compactified orthogonal gauge theory provide dark matter, and could the bifundamental connector make them observable? The relevant unknowns include confinement scales, stability, production, decay and reheating history.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0043"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb18318f7185a2e346392da2d7e83525f9c17e2717f58440d05ebc0cc48dd073","title":"Must an accelerating phase end before an initially sub-Planckian wavelength can stretch beyond the Hubble radius?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb4847778fdd586f8b258c2df85324de0da516aa7f00693d07b546ca7e9ce866","title":"Do analogous restrictions survive higher-dimensional cancellation mechanisms, and how strongly do the four-dimensional bounds constrain massive-vector models with heavy chiral anomaly cancellers?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0049"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cbb51aba7578bd4ae26514845034bb89d39cdc060bea0c1dbe7288989a25525d","title":"The model isolates how dimensionality and spectral correlations affect local landscape statistics. A homogeneous, isotropic Gaussian ensemble supplies a tractable baseline without identifying the ensemble with a particular compactification or quantum-gravity construction.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cbeca7c2f414ae5082d3bd7a22a6b8dab63530f13e41de96bf0e2c6e4ac91018","title":"The two allowed quantizations test whether thermal order depends on operator dimension. Removing the source mode allows a nonzero retained condensate to represent spontaneous Z2 breaking.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cba7c5d861531ea82bf4fbe9cf52d198efb90c4d995194e6a1b117caf9494b12","title":"How do de Sitter acceleration and its cosmological horizon modify semiclassical folded and spiky string Regge trajectories, their compatibility with the Higuchi bound and their ability to supply arbitrarily high spins?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0062"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb9a29628ee93d1928315e32b27d0a118d74bae21928879d7deaa529e267528e","title":"Does quantum gravity constrain the independent choice of EFT infrared and ultraviolet cutoffs, and which mass scale characterizes the resulting light spectrum when several towers have different gaps and degeneracies?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0070"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb84c88c5191450b89f19d24361ebb0109cd93c8d22c5c6f0aeb5b93a65af934","title":"Could the conserved axionic charge fragment into localized objects and thereby stop the homogeneous accelerating phase?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0074"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb2dccc7cfb4b8f43c268f54a54063ecffbf0ea6d2588ac2f4b1f236f243ddb3","title":"Can small post-inflationary radiation seeds prevent the LVS volume modulus from overshooting its vacuum, and what hierarchy between inflation and the weak scale makes this possible?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0075"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb197b0b9a01505681f1cc108073b97eb3fdbfdfbe7d63839a6e1f5caf790186","title":"How can flux potentials organize moduli stabilization and vacuum stability in type II/F-theory, and what constraints follow from tadpoles, scale separation and Swampland conjectures?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"des