etic solitonic and nonextremal black p-branes in arbitrary dimensions, and when do extremality, supersymmetry, electric-magnetic duality and nonsingularity coincide?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0118"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cbbdc38329a0b2f0b245f38e57f9713b9db3d1d44d12f46fb358a0269b6ee5d6","title":"Determine the quantum vacuum geometry, BPS masses and strong-coupling behavior of pure N=2 SU(2) gauge theory, and explain confinement after an N=1 perturbation.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0118"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb95eb9c9a2e4dfc478e7da2079600014e592a8c9f790932d740b44550510a13","title":"How should local mirror invariants of surfaces inside Calabi–Yau threefolds be defined, calculated in A- and B-models, and interpreted enumeratively, including suitable singular surfaces?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0121"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:cb9594c88880948870393dcce58e6a319d58df179bda807fffe5eb84c78d90c5","title":"How does circle compactification of quantum self-dual fields recover gravitational shifts in ordinary flux quantization: the Spin^c nature of a D4-brane gauge field from an M5-brane, and shifted Type IIA G₄ periods from the Type IIB self-dual G₅ field?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0121"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"}],"relations":[{"id":"source-access:c266b1e67b156f55284b146a","source":"q025-candidate-question:d836b647e03512ebe99c6abb","target":"source-question:cb19f7146b803c04638692cf162135e3f4f805fa770926c156c6d227054a79cb","detail":{"shardId":"relation-details-0039","recordSha256":"751114381fe37556609986d7419de3344371b28f0a426e0ff4bbdbe11882ce30"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-access:e1abf60d3712d4af4a5785b1","source":"q025-candidate-region:f1c244b7e3959d7ede8fc3d5","target":"source-ques